 scopes only 'reconcile-check and dry-run fetch/diff/preflight paths'; S3 Outcome scopes only 'write/apply and subprocess paths.'","S5 scopes only MCP and review-bot startup bindings.","Parent Scope: 'all affected CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers'; parent AC2 requires every affected consumer to receive an immutable binding with no in-progress reread.","Roster cross-check: no sibling's indented ACs deliver an authoritative (non-shadow) cutover of the ordinary CLI ticket/store command or the public Python library ticket-store operations.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"No sibling cuts the non-reconciler CLI ordinary ticket/store command path (and the public Python library operations) from shadow-only snapshot composition to AUTHORITATIVE runtime-binding consumption. S1 explicitly keeps execution on the legacy path ('Shadow composition does not control execution'; 'Existing execution remains authoritative'). S2 and S3 cut only the reconciler read/check and apply paths; S5 cuts MCP and review-bot; S4 cuts LLM; S6 cuts op-cert. The parent's Scope names 'all affected CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers' and AC2 requires 'Every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding and no in-progress operation rereads ambient state,' and AC1 requires CLI/Python to 'produce equivalent non-secret behavior from the approved precedence/root contract' — an authoritative, not shadow, guarantee.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc1511a05c96ddca1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11 (S1); owned-by-none gap across the roster","norm_id":"n941d5052d7141dc0","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add (or extend an existing child's scope for) an authoritative cutover of the non-reconciler CLI ticket/store commands and public Python library operations to consume the immutable OperationSnapshot binding with a no-in-progress-reread oracle, and pin its removal-precondition proof in S7.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion (or explicit child-test requirement) verifying Jira Cloud write scope drops DIG while preserving remaining required write scopes.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG'","AC5 covers bridge factories preserving auth lifecycles but does not name the DIG scope change","'Other auth, redaction, retry, TLS, and output behavior changes require an explicit child decision and test.'"],"finding":"The Explicit corrections state 'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG' as a concrete behavior delta, but no acceptance criterion covers verifying this scope removal (both that DIG is removed and that remaining scopes still function).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7289a6a1f68d494e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Explicit corrections; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n18d413dbf0984908","priority":0.8571,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A child implements bridge composition but silently retains DIG, or removes it without a test proving remaining write scope still works."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend AC5 or add an AC: 'Jira Cloud write composition no longer requests DIG scope, and bridge write operations succeed under the reduced scope set, verified by an offline oracle and bounded live canary.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1643,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Jira Cloud write scope loses `DIG`'","'tracker layout reaches every owner'","No AC line names DIG scope or tracker-layout propagation as a verified outcome"],"finding":"The 'Explicit corrections' list names concrete behavior changes — 'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG' and 'tracker layout reaches every owner' — that do not map to any acceptance criterion; the ACs cover precedence/root and consumer projections generally but no criterion verifies these specific deltas.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdca1870fc8a27a55","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > Explicit corrections; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n08a0fdcfd639eea1","priority":0.7857,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1643,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC5: 'Git and bridge factories preserve provider-native auth lifecycles and instantiate only the selected integration; missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback.'","S3 (6e3b) ACs name only DIG/Cloud-write-scope fail-closed and child-env; the Git push auth-lifecycle / fail-before-network outcome appears only in S3 Testing ('Failure-injection tests cover missing project/auth, revoked credential'), not as an AC.","S2 (e042) AC4 covers this outcome for Jira only; S5 (5851) AC3 covers it for review-bot Gerrit/GitHub only — neither exceeds scope to the reconciler/store Git push factory.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"Parent AC5's Git half is only partially covered: no child's acceptance criteria assert that the Git factory 'preserves provider-native auth lifecycles', 'instantiates only the selected integration', and that 'missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback' for Git specifically. S2 (e042) delivers this for the Jira bridge only, and S5 (5851) for review-bot Gerrit/GitHub only. S3 (6e3b) is the child that threads GitRuntime and owns Git adapter/ref/lock/push, but its enumerated ACs cover only (a) apply/Git/delivery paths completing with poisoned resolvers, (b) the Cloud-write/DIG fail-closed case, (c) child-env, (d) no-global-mutation, (e) provider-neutral regression, (f) facade rollback — none states the Git auth-lifecycle-preservation or the fail-before-Git-push-without-alternate-principal outcome as an acceptance criterion. S3 mentions 'revoked credential' only inside a Testing bullet, not as an AC oracle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f75bfee7f9fe88d68","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 (RP-04 S3); cross-checked against child e042 (S2) and child 5851 (S5)","norm_id":"n421d9d6195b28a91","priority":0.7857,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Promote S3's Git failure-injection scenario to an explicit S3 acceptance criterion mirroring S2 AC4 but scoped to GitRuntime/push (fail before network/write, no alternate-principal fallback, only selected integration, lifecycle preserved).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/config.md: a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11 & aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4 (no ordering edge)","docs/env-vars.md: 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 & 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 (no ordering edge)","docs/reuse-surface.md: 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 & bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06 (no ordering edge)","src/rebar/_store/push.py: 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 & 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 (no ordering edge)","tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py: 6f14-21a7-d806-44b2 & bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06 (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["9 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[operator-attested] AWS review-bot and reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live can' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2857,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries'","'reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries'","No definition of 'bounded' (count/cost/time)"],"finding":"Multiple ACs and design bullets require 'bounded live' canaries (e.g. 'bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries', 'bounded-live canaries') without stating the bound (request count, cost, or time), leaving the executor to guess the limit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f96396b4cf7aeb438","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (LLM cutover bullet; operator-attested bullet)","norm_id":"n5105038bbef98521","priority":0.3143,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a default such as 'bounded = at most N live requests per provider per canary run' to the plan.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm whether Langfuse/OTLP is composed on non-review-bot paths (CLI/Python/MCP/reconciler); if so, assign a child to prove its fail-open/no-op preservation there, else document it as review-bot-only.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4","G3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7094,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent Scope: 'Authentication is also composed inconsistently across LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, observability, and op-cert boundaries.'","Parent AC (box 8): 'observability's exception' documented; design: 'Preserve optional write-only Langfuse/OTLP/OTLP observability's fail-open/no-op behavior.'","S5 Plan step 3 scopes telemetry binding to the review-bot/MCP long-running startup only: 'Bind Langfuse/OTLP once at startup using provider-specific static input.'","S1/S2/S3 acceptance criteria and plans make no mention of observability/telemetry composition or its fail-open preservation.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"Non-review-bot observability (Langfuse/OTLP) composition may be owned by no child. The parent scope names 'observability' as an affected consumer and AC8-of-epic (box 8) plus the design require preserving optional write-only Langfuse/OTLP fail-open/no-op behavior application-wide, but only S5 (5851) claims observability binding, and it scopes that binding to review-bot startup ('Bind Langfuse/OTLP once at startup'). If observability is also initialized on CLI/Python/MCP or reconciler paths, no sibling's acceptance criteria assert its fail-open/no-op preservation there.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f130c39cdc3a666c1","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 5851-51d7-fda8-4966 (S5) — and absence across S1/S2/S3","norm_id":"n9ba41e9585d24101","priority":0.2406,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Observability is enabled in a CLI or plain reconciler run (not the AWS review-bot) and a partial/rejected telemetry credential is present; no child oracle proves the operation result is unchanged and telemetry is disabled fail-open in that path."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Either add an explicit acceptance criterion to S1 (or S3) covering observability fail-open/no-op preservation for non-review-bot paths, or state in the epic/S5 that observability is composed exclusively at long-running (review-bot/MCP) startup so S5 is the sole owner.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify that the epic-comment provenance recording is the epic's own attestation obligation (not a child deliverable), or assign S7 to consolidate child provenance into the epic comment.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC (final box): 'Epic comments record run/change IDs, timestamps, selected provider/auth-source kind, retry counts, and redacted outcomes.'","S5 records its provenance on the S5 ticket ('full evidence in the operator-attestation comment on this ticket'); S4/S6 likewise record on their own tickets.","S7 operator-attested AC records 'Live evidence includes run/change ids ...' but does not state the epic-comment aggregation obligation.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"The parent's operator-attested AC requires run/change IDs, timestamps, provider/auth-source kind, retry counts, and redacted outcomes to be recorded in EPIC comments, but no child owns recording aggregated provenance on the epic; each child records provenance only on its own ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffe1de9d775f305ee","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4 (S7) and child 5851-51d7-fda8-4966 (S5)","norm_id":"ne51647b939544328","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer verifies the epic's completion box and finds per-child provenance comments but no consolidated epic-level record of run/change IDs and outcomes."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a line to S7 (or the epic sequencing) making the aggregation of run/change IDs, timestamps, provider/auth-source kind, retry counts, and redacted outcomes into the epic comment an explicit S7 deliverable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likeliho